  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Title Screen",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Title Screen\"**\n\nThe profile is a game you have just switched on. The header is a 1200x500 title scene (the WAYSEL logotype, a sea, a dock with a rod, a goldfish swimming under a bobber that dips and pops a \"!\"), and below it each project is a numbered entry in the Fischdex, drawn as an RPG dialog window. Nothing is a web component pretending to be retro: every mark is an SVG rect path on a strict 4px game-pixel grid, rendered `crispEdges`, so the images stay sharp at any width GitHub gives them.\n\nThe world has two lighting states, not two themes. Dark mode is dusk (a banded, checker-dithered plum-to-orange sky, the sun half-set on the horizon, twinkling stars); light mode is midday (a pale blue sky, the sun high, no stars). The windows flip with it: dusk windows are ink panels with cream rules, midday windows are cream panels with ink rules. Density is that of a game menu: big lettering, short uppercase values, one idea per row.\n\nMotion is game motion: every animation runs on `steps()` timing so things move in whole pixels or blink, never ease. All of it stops under `prefers-reduced-motion`, which freezes the bite moment (the \"!\" shown, the fish parked under the bobber).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One typeface, Press Start 2P, rasterised to pixel paths at integer scales; no live text inside the images.",
      "4px game pixel as the unit of every coordinate, stroke, offset and animation step.",
      "Paired dusk / midday lighting states swapped through `<picture>` and `prefers-color-scheme`.",
      "Hand-authored sprites (16x9 goldfish; 14-wide project sprites) drawn from a fixed palette.",
      "Hard, stepped depth only: double pixel rules, 1-pixel lettering shadows, a 1-pixel button drop.",
      "Whole images are the links; no Markdown chrome beyond one intro paragraph and a credit line."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Lights Rule",
        "body": "Every asset ships as a dusk and a midday file generated from the same drawing with a different `THEMES` entry. A colour that only works in one light gets a per-light token, never a one-off.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Outline Rule",
        "body": "Every sprite is outlined in ink (#1b1430), in both lights. Outlines are what make a sprite read on either panel.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Integer Scale Rule",
        "body": "Lettering is drawn only at whole multiples of the 8px font cell (3x, 4x, 5x, 8x), so every font pixel lands on the 4px grid. No fractional sizes, no smoothing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Drawn Lettering Rule",
        "body": "Text inside images is pixel paths generated by `text()` in `assets/gen.py`, never an SVG `<text>` element or a referenced font; GitHub serves SVGs as images and would drop the font.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Game Pixel Rule",
        "body": "Every coordinate, size, offset and animation translation is a multiple of 4px. Anything that would land between pixels is snapped with `// P * P`.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Label Grid Rule",
        "body": "Project facts are always KEY / VALUE rows in a fixed key column, starting with NO. Facts are short uppercase phrases; a long value wraps to a second row with an empty key, never to a smaller size.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dither, Not Gradient Rule",
        "body": "Tonal transitions are flat bands joined by a 4px checker dither. A smooth gradient breaks the world.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** generate every asset from `assets/gen.py`, once per light, and regenerate both lights for any change.",
      "**Do** put every coordinate on the 4px game-pixel grid and draw lettering at integer multiples of the 8px font cell.",
      "**Do** log a new project as the next Fischdex number with a 14-wide ink-outlined sprite and NO. / TYPE / WHERE / LANG / DOES rows.",
      "**Do** animate with `steps()` timing in whole pixels, and stop every animation under `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "**Do** keep the goldfish as the mark: it swims in the title scene and owns the lead catch.",
      "**Do** write an `aria-label` and a matching `<img alt>` that says what the image says."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use rounded corners, blurs, soft shadows, glows, glass or smooth gradients anywhere in the images.",
      "**Don't** use emoji or icon-font glyphs; every symbol (the arrow, the \"!\", the bobber) is a drawn sprite.",
      "**Don't** set text in a second typeface or as live SVG `<text>`.",
      "**Don't** add badge walls, stats widgets, typing banners or invented counts; the Fischdex is the project list.",
      "**Don't** link a private repo; the lead catch links the live site."
    ]
  }
